{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnData3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnData3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburn3","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeMarkov3","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QSchurWeyl"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.markov_one_eq₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.markov_one_eq₃","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L172-L179","doc":"The abstract partition-function identity `tr_M(1) = ∑_λ d_λ w_λ`\n(`markov_one_eq`), now unconditional at `n = 3`: the conditional result of\n`QSchurWeyl.lean` applied to the bundle built above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeWedderburnData3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeWedderburnData3","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L147-L170","doc":"**The `HeckeWedderburnData` bundle for `H_3(q)`** (`q ≠ 0`, Ocneanu parameter\n`z`).  This discharges the hypothesis of every conditional result in\n`QSchurWeyl.lean` at `n = 3`.\n\nThe `markov_eq` field is the substance: `markovTrace3` is *defined* as the\nweighted character sum `w₀·χ_triv + w₁·χ_sign + w₂·χ_{(2,1)}`, and the bundle\ndemands `∑_λ w_λ · tr((iso h) λ)`.  These agree because the trace of a `1 × 1`\nblock is its single entry, so the two scalar blocks contribute their characters\ndirectly, while the `(2,1)` block contributes its matrix trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_one","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L137-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3_apply_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.piReshape3","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L84-L132","doc":"**The Π-reshape isomorphism** `ℝ × ℝ × M₂(ℝ) ≃ₐ[ℝ] ∏ l : Fin 3, M_{d_l}(ℝ)`.\n\nThis is pure bookkeeping — `M₁(ℝ) ≅ ℝ` on the two one-dimensional blocks — but it\nis what lets the binary-product Wedderburn iso of `wedderburn3` meet the\nindexed-product shape that `HeckeWedderburnData.iso` demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.reshapeInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.reshapeInv","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The inverse reshape: read the single entry out of each `1 × 1` block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.entry11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.entry11","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L72-L77","doc":"The single entry of a `1 × 1` block.  The index is built from the width\nhypothesis rather than from a numeral: `(0 : Fin (heckeDim3 l))` cannot be\nelaborated, because instance synthesis works at reducible transparency and will\nnot evaluate `heckeDim3 0` down to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.reshapeFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.reshapeFun","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L63-L70","doc":"The forward reshape: the two scalar blocks become `1 × 1` matrices, the\nseminormal block is carried across unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_two","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_one","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3_zero","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WedderburnData3.heckeDim3","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeWedderburnData3.lean#L52-L55","doc":"The Wedderburn block dimensions of `H_3(q)`, indexed by the three partitions\nof `3`: `d_{(3)} = 1` (trivial), `d_{(1,1,1)} = 1` (sign), `d_{(2,1)} = 2` (the\nseminormal block).  `1² + 1² + 2² = 6 = 3!`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}